    misreading: "Do not read the prophets' weeping as despair. David ends with God's promise — come back to Us and We will accept you — and John's weeping carries him across the desert to the Garden.",
    reflection: "Ask whether you have ever felt the loneliness David describes after doing something wrong.",
    audit: ["Do I feel safe from God's plan?", "Do I remember my slips?", "Have I felt the intimacy of obedience?", "What would make me weep like John?"],
